%% One installation per account. [outside] = AWS console/CLI, IAM, or time.
%% Federation (on/off) and networking (fixed at create) are orthogonal attributes of Deployed/Ready.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> Empty
    Empty --> Authorised: [outside] attach rendered deployer policy
    Authorised --> Deployed: admin setup (any region, parent AMI resolved there)
    Authorised --> RolledBack: admin setup, create fails
    RolledBack --> Residue: admin teardown
    Deployed --> Ready: admin build-image
    Deployed --> Deployed: admin setup (update)
    Ready --> Ready: admin build-image [--extension] (rebuild in place)<br/>admin setup (update, image carried forward)
    Ready --> Ready: admin setup --region B — refused, names the bucket's region<br/>build-image from an older-base CLI — refused, upgrade the CLI
    Ready --> Dangling: [outside] AMI deregistered
    Dangling --> Ready: admin build-image
    Ready --> Busy: baas run (job item launching…running)
    Busy --> Ready: instance records outcome + self-terminates<br/>Ctrl+C hook · poll cap · jobs terminate · watchdog
    Busy --> Busy: admin teardown refused (names job ids)
    Deployed --> Residue: admin teardown [--delete-bucket]
    Ready --> Residue: admin teardown [--delete-bucket]<br/>(saves the extension, retires the image)
    Residue --> Residue: admin setup refused (bucket or table exists)
    Residue --> Empty: [outside] delete table<br/>(+ bucket without --delete-bucket)

    state Residue {
        [*] --> kept
        kept: results table (always)<br/>bucket (unless --delete-bucket)
    }
